inal color-lookup rule.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/88e364bc/D2/1/code.py:59:    - Same wall color across different quadrants but different motion directions is the primary visual\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/0934a4d8/D13/2/code.py:163:    The symmetry no longer lives at the whole-grid level. The marker is a locator for a smaller symmetric panel, so the solver must switch reference frames: crop first, then restore inside the crop.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code_combo/67e490f4/8/code.py:68:#     - The remaining shapes are also rotationally symmetric, so the D7 restriction is visible across the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b10624e5/D13/2/code.py:69:- Divider color is excluded from motif colors so the cross separator remains visually unique.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b10624e5/D13/2/code.py:107:    \"\"\"Return the unique full-row/full-col divider intersection.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b10624e5/D13/2/code.py:138:    Copy an internal anchor overlay across quadrants with scaling and reflection.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/88e364bc/D14/1/code.py:13:#      becomes \"..04 0\" across the wall contact: the yellow still ends at the same interior cell, but\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/abc82100/D10/0/code.py:49:# - Legends are scored to spread across the board, while still keeping enough nearby free cells\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/abc82100/D10/0/code.py:123:    - Rule examples are scattered across the same general area as the ordinary source pixels,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8698868d/D15/0/code.py:67:#       - across examples, users can see more sprite candidates than frame slots\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/62593bfd/D1/3/code.py:75:#       Across examples, top objects match by rotation only; mirrored \"handedness\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/8698868d/D15/1/code.py:43:- We avoid duplicated hole-counts across frames because that would introduce a second cardinality change (many-to-one matc