bject settles\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/20270e3b/D3/2/code.py:30:#   in 1..3 with repeated support across samples, so matching is not too free-form.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/20270e3b/D3/2/code.py:41:#   Across 2-4 examples a human can see that extra colored specks/mini-blocks appear in different places\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/edb79dae/D4/3/code.py:50:#      original overlapping legend. Both are repeated across multiple placements and colors.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/5545f144/D22/0/code.py:34:     sprite cells across every simulated state, avoid touching any other marker,\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7ed72f31/D5/0/code.py:13:    - Row/column red lines reflect monochrome payloads across the line.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7ed72f31/D5/0/code.py:53:      across groups, so blockers of a different color are never accidentally mirrored by another group.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/7ed72f31/D5/0/code.py:61:      preventing cross-group contact, overlap, and out-of-bounds placements.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D11/1/code.py:25:      marker color is reused across the distractors and is not used by any anchor.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/5dbc8537/D1/0/code.py:74:#    The cue colors are reused across different sizes but are unique within any one\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/5dbc8537/D1/0/code.py:87:#      be recovered from any stripe-adjacent bg cell by extending across rows whose\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/581f7754/D3/3/code.py:28:#   - `find_components(..., connectivity=8)` remains necessary; switching to 4-connectivity would incorrectly\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/20270e3b/D10/1/code.py:37:#   Across samples the shared connector color changes, while body color stays yellow. In each\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/20270e3b/D10/1/code.py:38:#   input, the only repeated connector color across the two sprites predicts which bars line up\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/