/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D2/1/code.py:156:    \"\"\"Return the center of an exact 5-pixel cross component, else None.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D2/1/code.py:168:    Recolor rectangles whose opposite corners are indicated by same-color cross markers.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D2/1/code.py:173:    - Away from the legend, an active marker color appears as two separate 5-pixel crosses.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D2/1/code.py:178:    - If two exact crosses are present, use their centers as opposite corners of an axis-aligned rectangle.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D2/1/code.py:184:      two cross shapes. Because each cross sticks out by one cell in four directions, center recovery is the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D2/1/code.py:218:            center = _cross_center(comp)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D2/1/code.py:219:            assert center is not None, \"every active marker component must be an exact 5-pixel cross\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D2/1/code.py:222:        assert len(centers) == 2, \"every active marker color must contain exactly two crosses\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D2/1/code.py:226:        assert rmin < rmax and cmin < cmax, \"cross centers must be diagonal corners\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D2/1/code.py:250:# ── CFG: cross-pair rectangle shape ────────────────────────────────\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D2/1/code.py:265:def _cross_cells(center_r: int, center_c: int) -> list[tuple[int, int]]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D2/1/code.py:269:def _cross_pair_cells(rmin: int, cmin: int, rmax: int, cmax: int, diag: str) -> list[tuple[int, int]]:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D2/1/code.py:270:    \"\"\"Return the 10 cells for a pair of crosses whose centers sit on one rectangle diagonal.\"\"\"\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/9385bd28/D2/1/code.py:277:       