D19/2/code.py:71:      causal link visually localized and easy to compare across examples.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/6e453dd6/D19/2/code.py:182:    - For each emitting cavity, read its unique non-background marker color and paint that color across the entire right side on every row covered by the cavity.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/b5ca7ac4/D13/1/code.py:21:#      right-moving group. The swatch colors swap across generated examples, so the\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/247ef758/D5/0/code.py:50:#   stamp fits after clipping. Row/col marks remain unique across mover colors, reducing ambiguity in target matching.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/247ef758/D5/0/code.py:57:# - Across only 2-4 examples, a human can now see three repeated cues for each mover color:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/247ef758/D5/0/code.py:61:#   switch that would require more examples to infer.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/142ca369/D4/1/code.py:41:#    Every generated sample contains at least one bounce, and bounced rays keep crossing beside walls whose color\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/142ca369/D4/1/code.py:42:#    differs from the ray color. Across 2-4 examples this should make the new rule legible: walls redirect rays\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D6/1/code.py:23:#   1. a large cross: full middle row + full middle column (9 cells)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D6/1/code.py:26:#   the resting shape (large cross), while the missing complement (corner-star)\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D6/1/code.py:28:#   large cross to the far endpoint. A pre-placed large cross is already stable.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D6/1/code.py:31:#   variant: solid 5x5 at top -> top large cross, bottom corner-star\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D6/1/code.py:36:# - The two complementary results are still few and repeated across channels:\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D6/1/code.py:37:#   every sample shows several large crosses and several corner-stars, which is\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D6/1/code.py:39:# - The corner-star is disconnected under 4-connectivity, while the cross is\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D6/1/code.py:46:#   disconnected 1-cell pieces. The new passive cross is a connected 9-cell\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D6/1/code.py:48:# - Shape detection can no longer rely on a colored top-left cell: the cross has\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D6/1/code.py:53:#   bounds and leave room for the existing crossover network.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D6/1/code.py:54:# - The 4-cell endpoint gap keeps passive large crosses detached from wires.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D6/1/code.py:57:#   of 3x3 squares, and outputs contain large crosses / four-corner clusters.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D6/1/code.py:65:# - Passive large crosses are isolated from the wire mask.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D6/1/code.py:278:    - The background is the dominant color. Non-background cells are either wire elements (8/5/9) or 5×5-scale tokens near wire endpoints: a solid 5×5 block, a corner-star made of four 2×2 corner chunks, or an already-settled large cross.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D6/1/code.py:281:    - Every solid 5×5 block is replaced in place by the large cross (middle row + middle column), and its complementary corner-star is sent to the far endpoint of the same wire component.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D6/1/code.py:282:    - Every corner-star token stays where it is and sends the large cross to the opposite endpoint. Pre-placed large crosses are stable and remain unchanged.\n/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ceshi/code/a47bf94d/D6/1/code.py:285:    - Inside a 5×5 square, the solid token decomposes exactly into two complementary pieces: a 9-cell cross and sixteen corner cells. The wire network only decides where the